{"id":"2656a300-1133-4cbd-8a30-29c90ab455ce","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The Java main method always receives a non-null array for args, even if it is empty, according to the Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466101Z"}
{"id":"34f613c3-3c0c-445b-958e-c47d92cd6a5a","expr":"b == 0 || (a / b) * b + (a % b) == a","rationale":"If b is not zero, integer division and modulus reconstruct a, otherwise division not evaluated.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466240Z"}
{"id":"96953bd0-f4b6-4a21-bd3e-52064ed2585f","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The Java runtime guarantees that the parameter 'args' to main is never null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466333Z"}
{"id":"07cf32ba-6a9c-4875-9acc-0bae92df1321","expr":"b == 0 || b > Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"For all nonzero b, b may not be Integer.MIN_VALUE if special handling is required for edge-case division.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466240Z"}
{"id":"bb24e5b3-5bd3-462f-8403-dbb79111e8d6","expr":"(b == 0) == (result == Integer.MIN_VALUE)","rationale":"If b==0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE; otherwise, it returns the division result.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.467984Z"}
{"id":"0bbedfda-811b-4137-8420-8bf494190169","expr":"b == 0 || a / b <= a","rationale":"For positive b, integer division result is less than or equal to a; safe because b == 0 is guarded.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466240Z"}
{"id":"790b1afb-eb1d-4f01-949a-b4fa8296e872","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Arrays in Java always have a non-negative length, including zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466333Z"}
{"id":"bcdef99d-55ec-4700-bce8-6ec9e3697d75","expr":"(b != 0) == (result == a / b)","rationale":"If b is not zero, the method returns the integer division of a by b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.467984Z"}
{"id":"67dfa954-4711-465c-ad4b-c24461e42fd1","expr":"args.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The 'args' parameter is always an array at this method point.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.466333Z"}
{"id":"f6e74870-d6aa-4c3f-ac79-42778fdb592a","expr":"(b == 0) || (result == a / b)","rationale":"If b==0, result need not equal a/b, but if not, it must be a/b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.467984Z"}
{"id":"808d0f12-669c-4dbe-b58e-dc17ab337862","expr":"(b != 0) || (result == Integer.MIN_VALUE)","rationale":"If b==0, result is Integer.MIN_VALUE; otherwise, this is vacuously true.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-18T06:33:13.467984Z"}
